  "target": "Members of public medical insurance who, for unavoidable reasons, paid the full amount of medical costs at the counter of a medical institution (for example, eligibility could not be confirmed so care was paid for privately, care was received under a different insurance eligibility and the medical costs were repaid, or a person aged 70 or over paid a higher share than the applicable rate). It also covers people who had a therapeutic appliance such as a corset, or therapeutic glasses for conditions such as amblyopia in children, made on a physician's instruction, and people who paid for a transfusion of fresh blood.",
