  "benefit": "Sign language interpreters, note-takers, interpreter-guides for deafblind people, communication supporters for people with aphasia and others are dispatched to settings such as hospital visits, administrative procedures, school meetings and community gatherings. For people with visual impairments, support such as writing and reading on their behalf, braille transcription and audio transcription is also provided. Some municipal counters have a sign language interpreter on site, and remote sign language interpretation may be available.",
